Part 1: String Manipulation Script
Description

In this section, the program asks the user to enter a sentence. It then performs several operations on the entered text and displays the results.

Operations Performed

Find Sentence Length

Calculates the total number of characters in the sentence using len().

Convert Text Case

Converts the sentence to uppercase using upper().
Converts the sentence to lowercase using lower().

Reverse the Sentence

Uses string slicing ([::-1]) to display the sentence in reverse order.

Count Words

Splits the sentence into words using split().
Counts the number of words present.

Display First and Last Word

Extracts the first and last words from the sentence.

Palindrome Check

Removes leading and trailing spaces.
Converts the text to lowercase.
Compares the string with its reversed version to determine whether it is a palindrome.

Part 2: Simple Calculator
Description

This section of the program functions as a basic calculator. It accepts two numbers from the user and performs multiple arithmetic operations.

Operations Performed
Operation	Symbol	DescriptionAddition	+	Adds two numbers
Subtraction	-	Finds the difference
Multiplication	*	Multiplies two numbers
Division	/	Performs normal division
Exponentiation	**	Raises first number to the power of second
Floor Division	//	Returns the quotient without decimal values
Modulus	%	Returns the remainder